  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Udemy’s transformation is dominated by its completed merger with Coursera, creating a unified global skills platform. The combined entity is pivoting to a subscription model in the AI upskilling arms race, deliberately trading top-line momentum for longer-term margin structure. Standalone demand was under pressure heading into the deal, with revenue contracting and losses deepening. New AI-powered features (Role Play, Altus) signal a push into enterprise-scale generative AI training, while the merger reshapes competitive dynamics by consolidating two major education-technology marketplaces.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Management executed a high-stakes merger with Coursera and committed to a subscription-first strategy that prioritizes recurring revenue quality over near-term growth. Aggressive investment in AI-driven learning tools and the Altus platform demonstrates a playbook built on capturing the enterprise skills wave. Credibility remains under scrutiny: the sharp share-price slide and widening losses in the standalone pre-merger period highlight execution risk, even as the combined entity’s long-term narrative hinges on integration, margin improvement, and the conviction behind the AI-centered subscription pivot.",
